<Base title="Our Programs" description="Explore the four pillars of GEAR Moto Foundation: Gear, Education, Assistance, and Recovery.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Our four pillars</div><h1>Gear. Education.<br/><span class="accent">Assistance. Recovery.</span></h1><p class="lede" style="color:#e5e8eb">Four connected commitments to support riders before a crash and through the challenges that may follow.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap prose"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#D71920">G · Gear</div><h2>Protective Gear Access</h2><p>Our proposed Gear program will help qualifying riders access essential protective equipment, including compliant helmets, armored riding apparel, gloves, and boots. Planned delivery methods include partner discounts, vouchers, donated equipment, and direct-to-vendor awards, subject to funding and approved eligibility policies.</p>
<div class="eyebrow" style="color:#D71920">E · Education</div><h2>Rider Education</h2><p>Education will focus on access to new-rider training, advanced and returning-rider courses, endorsement-related education, and relevant road-safety or first-aid learning. Proposed awards will use objective, need-based criteria and approved training providers.</p>
<div class="eyebrow" style="color:#D71920">A · Assistance</div><h2>Rider & Family Assistance</h2><p>After a serious motorcycle crash, unexpected expenses can strain an entire household. The proposed Assistance program may help qualifying applicants with uncovered medical or rehabilitation bills, essential living costs, temporary income disruption, transportation, or mobility needs. Awards would depend on documented hardship, available funds, and formally adopted grant criteria—not friendship, club membership, or a donor's preferred recipient.</p>
<div class="eyebrow" style="color:#D71920">R · Recovery</div><h2>Recovery & Reconnection</h2><p>Recovery isn't simply returning to a motorcycle. We aim to connect riders and families with credible recovery resources, community support, and practical assistance to help stabilize and rebuild after a crash. Every rider chooses their own timeline and whether to ride again.</p>
<div class="program-callout"><strong>Program launch status:</strong> All four pillars are in development. Applications, award amounts, selection requirements, and opening dates have not yet been announced.</div><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/contact/">Ask About GEAR</a><a class="btn btn-outline-dark" href="/get-help/">Get Help Information</a></div></div></section>
</Base>
